p-adic-section-conjecture-October-6-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":31,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a1aa4a9be27f383ee80401f928dd265b702bd494b84377217d342f783fe358de","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-p-adic-section-conjecture-October-6-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d04790018e79c62b1a113b4892068ff55c6aef756f548778498c679076043738","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-p-adic-section-conjecture-October-6-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L31"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:section}\nFor every prime $p$, every finite extension $k/\\mathbb Q_p$, and every\nsmooth proper geometrically connected curve $X/k$ of genus at least two,\nthe map\n\\[\n X(k)\\longrightarrow\n \\left\\{\\begin{gathered}\n s:G_k\\to\\pi_1(X)\\text{ a continuous group homomorphism}\\\\\n \\text{such that }(\\pi_1(X)\\to G_k)\\circ s=\\mathrm{id}_{G_k}\n \\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\big/\\pi_1(X_{\\bar k})\n\\]\nis bijective. The quotient is by conjugation by the full geometric\n\\'etale fundamental group."}
